      "text": "Dialysis (Visking) tubing is an artificial partially permeable membrane with pore sizes of approximately $2.5\\,\\text{nm}$. Glucose molecules have a diameter of about $1.5\\,\\text{nm}$ and can pass through the pores in the membrane."
